From: c0de-coffee <53132135+c0de-coffee@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:58:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] session: Read the EIS keymap from the start

The keymap fd may share its file offset with other clients. KWin sends
the same keymap file to every EIS client, so once a client has read it,
the next one reads from the end and gets nothing: grd fails with
"Keyboard layout was empty" and drops the connection. With KWin this
happens on every reconnection to a session, since grd connects to its
EIS server again.

Use pread() at offset 0.
---
 src/grd-session.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/grd-session.c b/src/grd-session.c
index c2a8682..ab372aa 100644
--- a/src/grd-session.c
+++ b/src/grd-session.c
@@ -1278,7 +1278,9 @@ setup_xkb_keymap (GrdSession        *session,
     {
       int ret;
 
-      ret = read (ei_keymap_get_fd (keymap), buf, keymap_size);
+      /* The fd may be shared with other clients, so its offset can be
+       * anywhere: always read from the start. */
+      ret = pread (ei_keymap_get_fd (keymap), buf, keymap_size, 0);
       if (ret > 0)
         {
           break;
